# === C Brain — what must NEVER be committed =========================
# Rule: the engine travels, lived experience does not.
# This file is the SECOND net. The first is sync.sh's allowlist
# (deny by default), the third is leakcheck.py (which blocks the commit).

# --- The user's lived content: never inside the engine ---
# ANCHORED AT THE ROOT (`/`): without the leading slash, git applies the pattern
# at EVERY level and also excludes `skeleton/lessons/`, `skeleton/meta/`… — so
# the empty-trunk skeleton never shipped in the repo, and the install failed on
# the user's machine. Caught by installing from a real clone, never from a copy.
/state/
/lessons/
/projects/
/meta/
/life/
/sessions/
/corpus/
/audits/
/MEMORY.md

# --- Regenerated artefacts holding the FULL TEXT of the notes ---
# planet/graph.json is over a megabyte and carries real names from the notes.
# It is rebuilt on every launch by graph_export.py.
planet/graph.json

# --- Machine-specific (contains a hardcoded home path) ---
hooks/com.claudebrain.resume.plist
*.plist
!*.plist.template

# --- Dead weight / dependencies ---
capsule/node_modules/
capsule/assets/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- System ---
.DS_Store
